      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The numerical optimizer agrees with $\\bar{Y}$ to six decimal places, as expected.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Poisson Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "The simple model above assumes every firm shares the same patent rate $\\lambda$ — clearly too restrictive. Older firms may have different rates than newer ones; firms in the Northeast may differ from those in the South. Poisson regression relaxes this by letting $\\lambda$ vary across firms as a function of their characteristics:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Y_i \\sim \\text{Poisson}(\\lambda_i), \\qquad \\lambda_i = \\exp(X_i'\\beta)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "We use $\\exp(\\cdot)$ as the link function because $\\lambda_i$ must be strictly positive, but $X_i'\\beta$ can be any real number. The exponential maps the linear predictor onto the positive real line.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Building the covariate matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "The design matrix $X$ includes:\n",
        "- An **intercept** column of ones\n",
        "- **Firm age** and **age squared** — the relationship between age and patenting is likely nonlinear (young firms ramp up, very old ones may stagnate), so including the quadratic term lets the model capture that curvature\n",
        "- **Region dummies** for Northeast, Northwest, South, and Southwest, with Midwest as the omitted baseline — we must drop one region to avoid perfect collinearity with the intercept\n",
        "- The **customer indicator** — the variable we care most about"
      ],
      "id": "55011881"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "region_dummies = pd.get_dummies(df[\"region\"], drop_first=True, prefix=\"region\").astype(float)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = pd.concat([\n",
        "    pd.Series(1.0, index=df.index, name=\"const\"),\n",
        "    df[[\"age\", \"iscustomer\"]].astype(float),\n",
        "    region_dummies\n",
        "], axis=1)\n",
        "X.insert(2, \"age_sq\", (df[\"age\"] ** 2).astype(float))\n",
        "\n",
        "Y_reg = df[\"patents\"].astype(float)"
      ],
      "id": "a05b705d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Log-likelihood for Poisson regression\n",
        "\n",
        "The log-likelihood extends naturally from the simple case — we just replace the scalar $\\lambda$ with the vector $\\lambda_i = \\exp(X_i'\\beta)$:"
      ],
      "id": "3c6408a4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "def poisson_reg_loglik(beta, Y, X):\n",
        "    Xb  = np.clip(X.values @ beta, -50, 50)   # clip for numerical stability\n",
        "    lam = np.exp(Xb)\n",
        "    return np.sum(Y * np.log(lam + 1e-300) - lam)"
      ],
      "id": "61f7c9e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Finding the MLE with `scipy.optimize`"
      ],
      "id": "a5aff7db"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "beta_init = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
        "\n",
        "res = optimize.minimize(\n",
        "    lambda b: -poisson_reg_loglik(b, Y_reg, X),\n",
        "    beta_init,\n",
        "    method=\"BFGS\",\n",
        "    options={\"maxiter\": 5000}\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_optim = res.x"
      ],
      "id": "77702f2d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "print(\"Optimization converged:\", res.success)\n",
        "print(\"Coefficients:\", dict(zip(X.columns, beta_optim.round(5))))"
      ],
      "id": "df163130",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Checking against `statsmodels`"
      ],
      "id": "adb3ff0e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "glm_model  = sm.GLM(Y_reg, X, family=sm.families.Poisson())\n",
        "glm_result = glm_model.fit()"
      ],
      "id": "65726ac9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "coef_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Variable\":       [\"Intercept\", \"Age\", \"Age²\", \"Customer\",\n",
        "                       \"Region: Northeast\", \"Region: Northwest\",\n",
        "                       \"Region: South\", \"Region: Southwest\"],\n",
        "    \"Coefficient\":    glm_result.params.values,\n",
        "    \"Std. Error\":     glm_result.bse.values,\n",
        "    \"z-statistic\":    glm_result.tvalues.values,\n",
